{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instArchimedeanInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instArchimedeanInfinitesimal","kind":"instance","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L130-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instReebPositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.instReebPositive","kind":"instance","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L127-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ArchimedeanInfinitesimal.archimedean_smallness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ArchimedeanInfinitesimal.archimedean_smallness","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L124-L124","doc":"For every standard real `λ > 0` and every `n : ℕ`, the\noperator-order value `b ≥ 0` realising `n · ε` satisfies\n`b ≤ λ` (uniformly in `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ArchimedeanInfinitesimal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ArchimedeanInfinitesimal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ArchimedeanInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ArchimedeanInfinitesimal","kind":"class","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L101-L125","doc":"**§3b primary conjecture class — archimedean smallness of `ε`.**\n\n`@conjecture: primary`\n\nFor every standard real `λ > 0` and every `n : ℕ`, the `n`-fold\niterate `n · ε` is dominated by `λ · 𝟙` in the operator order on\n`End(A)`.  The operator order is a real-valued comparison at the\narchimedean layer, so the field is stated against real parameters:\nfor every `λ > 0` and every `n` there is an operator-order value\n`b ≥ 0` realising `n · ε` with `b ≤ λ`.  Concrete content: the\nbound is uniform in `n` (the defining archimedean-infinitesimal\nsmallness — `n · ε` never escapes any standard `λ`).\n\nThis matches Conway's definition of a positive infinitesimal in\n`𝐍𝐨` under `ε ↦ 1/ω`.  No instance is supplied: this is the\nhonest open state of the archimedean-smallness conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebPositive.pairing_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebPositive.pairing_pos","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L99-L99","doc":"For every non-zero state-norm `nv`, the Frobenius-pairing value\n`p = ⟨v, ε·v⟩` is strictly positive and bounded by `nv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebPositive.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebPositive.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebPositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebPositive","kind":"class","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L78-L99","doc":"**§3b primary conjecture class — positivity of `ε`.**\n\n`@conjecture: primary`\n\nUnder the Frobenius pairing `⟨·,·⟩`, every non-zero state `v` has\n`⟨v, ε·v⟩ > 0`.  The pairing is a real-valued functional living at\nthe archimedean layer, so the field is stated against the real\n*state-norm* parameter `nv = ‖v‖`: for every `nv > 0` there is a\nstrictly positive pairing value `p = ⟨v, ε·v⟩` bounded by the\nnorm.  Concrete content: the pairing value is strictly positive\n(not merely `≠ 0`) and scales with the state — the shape that\ndistinguishes a *positive* infinitesimal from an arbitrary one.\n\nNo instance is supplied: this is the honest open state of the\npositivity conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.epsilon_ne_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.epsilon_ne_id","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L76-L76","doc":"`ε` is non-trivial: distinct from the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.epsilon","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The Reeb infinitesimal `ε : A ⟶ A` as an endomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.obj","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The substrate object `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon","kind":"structure","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebEpsilon.lean#L53-L76","doc":"**ReebEpsilon**: the Reeb infinitesimal on a substrate with a\ncategorical Reeb derivation.\n\nEncoded as a bundled structure rather than a field, because the\nconcrete construction via `d/dt|_{t=0} Φ_t` requires the\none-parameter Reeb flow, which is not yet formalised at the\ncategorical level.  The structure carries the *data* of `ε`; its\ntwo defining *properties* (positivity, archimedean smallness) are\nthe primary-conjecture classes `ReebPositive` /\n`ArchimedeanInfinitesimal` below — they live at the archimedean\n(real-valued pairing / operator order) layer and so are stated\nagainst real parameters.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:reeb-epsilon}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:reeb-epsilon","label":"def:reeb-epsilon","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/reeb-epsilon.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}